# Components and React

Create small, focused components with one clear responsibility. Do not put API calls, business logic, forms, tables, modals, filters, and multiple UI sections in one huge page.

Extract only when it improves readability. Do **not** split ~10 lines of simple JSX into a new component. Not everything must be a component.

Prefer composition over giant configurable components with many boolean flags (`showHeader`, `isAdmin`, `isMobile`). Keep component APIs simple. Avoid excessive props.

## React

Functional components. Follow Rules of Hooks — never call hooks conditionally. Avoid unnecessary `useEffect` and state. Prefer derived values.

```tsx
// BAD
const [filtered, setFiltered] = useState([]);
useEffect(() => { setFiltered(users.filter(...)); }, [users]);

// GOOD
const filtered = users.filter(...);
```

Keep state local. Lift only when required. Do not add Redux, Zustand, Context, or React Query without a reason. One authoritative source of truth — do not duplicate server data in client state.

## Server → Client payloads

Pass only the fields the Client Component needs. Do not send entire database objects across the boundary.

## Client-side fetching

Not the default. Use client fetch (useEffect, SWR, React Query) only for live updates, polling, infinite scroll, user-triggered fetch, client-only or realtime data.

## Forms

Validate input (reuse existing schemas). Handle loading, prevent duplicate submit, show meaningful errors, disable actions when appropriate. Critical validation must also run on the server.

## UI states

Every important UI: loading, error, empty, disabled, success, hover, focus, responsive, mobile, accessibility. Lists/tables need loading, empty, error, and success separately when necessary.

## Accessibility and SEO

Semantic HTML (`button`, `a`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `header`, `footer`, `form`, `label`). Labels on inputs, keyboard access, real links, alt text, visible focus. Color is not the only signal.

Public pages: Server Components, static/ISR when appropriate, Metadata API, server-rendered SEO content, meaningful titles/descriptions.

## Images

Use `next/image` with width, height, sizes, priority, and quality when suitable. Do not load huge images unnecessarily.
